{#-
  Task 8 (phase 6): the public agenda feed -- iCalendar (RFC 5545), a
  different format for a different consumer from feed.njk's own RSS
  syndication feed above. A calendar client subscribes to this address
  once; the scheduled editions it lists, their times and the event page
  each one points to arrive on their own at every later rebuild, with
  nothing to administer and no account -- the shared-calendar request
  named in F-06 (spec §4).

  All the real work -- filtering to `scheduled` editions, the Europe/Paris
  DST-aware start time, RFC 5545 TEXT escaping and 75-octet line folding,
  and why UID/LOCATION/URL all carry the event page's own address and
  never the meeting room -- is `agendaCalendar` and the functions it
  calls, in site/.eleventy.js: a single filter call, like feed.njk's own
  `eventDescription` and `rfc822` above it, rather than template logic of
  its own. `| safe` is required, not decorative: `agendaCalendar` already
  returns a fully RFC 5545-escaped and folded string (backslash-escaping,
  not HTML entities), and Nunjucks' own default auto-escaping would
  otherwise turn every literal "&" this feed writes into "&amp;", which is
  meaningless -- and wrong -- inside an iCalendar file. The same "already
  serialised, mark it safe" contract event.njk's own `| jsonLd | safe`
  already uses for the identical reason, one property syntax over.

  Line endings: RFC 5545 requires CRLF throughout, unlike this file's own
  front matter and this one line of template markup. `agendaCalendar`
  already returns pure CRLF, but this file, or Eleventy's own handling of
  it, still contributes whatever line ending it itself ends on -- so
  purity is enforced once more, on the actual rendered bytes, by the
  `crlfForCalendarFeeds` transform (site/.eleventy.js): see that
  transform's own comment for why the belt is not made redundant by the
  braces.
-#}
